                <pb facs="0590" n="496" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg496"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.12/1198: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morrow</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-07-17T14:00:00-04:00">July 17, 1930—2
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>182. Department’s 176, July 11, 1 p.m.,<anchor n="28" xml:id="d462-f1"/> and your
                    148, July 16, 4 p.m. You are authorized to initiate concurrent yet independent
                    negotiations when you consider it expedient to do so for (1) an en bloc
                    settlement of claims and (2) Rio Grande rectification with related
                    questions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
